    ],
    "return_type": "Result<AsyncFd<T>, AsyncFdRegisterError<T>>; conversion to io::Error drops the retained inner owner on failure."
  },
  "safety_argument": [
    "PtyIo clones the caller-owned descriptor into an OwnedFd while its owner is live, verifies and sets O_NONBLOCK, then moves that owner into File and AsyncFd. The private field is shared through Arc; reader/writer tasks receive references only and never close or replace the registered descriptor.",
    "Both AsyncSocket and AsyncDatagramSocket move an owned socket2::Socket into their private AsyncFd after set_nonblocking(true). They expose no get_mut replacement path. Their into_inner calls AsyncFd::into_inner, which deregisters before returning the owned Socket.",
    "Read/write interest, readiness I/O, EOF handling and error propagation are unchanged. PTY still catches a missing-I/O-driver panic and returns the same error. Register failure converts to io::Error and drops its retained owner, matching the prior constructor behavior."
  ],
